<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Progressive Reform Party (Suriname)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vooruitstrevende Hervormings Partij, United Hindustani Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Progressive Reform Party (VHP) is a Surinamese political party founded in 1949 as the United Hindustani Party under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagernath-lachmon">Jagernath Lachmon</a>, and renamed in 1973. It has drawn its support chiefly from the Indo-Surinamese community and has taken part in many coalition governments. Under Chan Santokhi it led the government from 2020 to 2025.</p></div>
